  "name": "ACTH (ADRENOCORTICOTROPIC HORMONE)",
  "code": "1732",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p><strong>COMMENT:</strong></p>\n<p><br>-ACTH is a hormone produced in the pituitary and stimulates steroid production in adrenal cortex. Its secretion is controlled by the&nbsp;hypothalamic CRF and by negative feedback from cortisol.<br>-ACTH values are valuable in differential diagnosis of adrenal insufficiency/hypersecretion. In primary adrenal insufficiency, elevated levels&nbsp;and typical low levels are the rule when adrenal insufficiency is secondary to pituitary dysfunction.<br>-ACTH determination can also help to identify the cause of cortisol hypersecretion in Cushing&rsquo;s syndrome. ACTH levels are lowered when it is&nbsp;due to lesion of hyperplasia of adrenal cortex and high when it is due to ectopic ACTH production or pituitary hypersecretion.</p>",
